# Present finite money domain and future extraction gate

Current exact frozen observer→closed-money admissible domain is EMPTY: official reviewed observer predicates define raw usage.cost and token counts but no exact category extraction schema. Therefore observedCategories=[] and closed createResolver.money must return UNKNOWN/missing-evidence; cost0 is not qualified zero. Capture reruns observer and preserves UNKNOWN/fullK/STOP. Do not copy diagnostic raw usage.categories, infer inference, accept caller categories/proof, or amend actual registry EMPTY. Mock-resolver full-money positives remain conditional algebra tests, not supported closed pipeline proof. This is an explicit unresolved actual-money pipeline/qualification blocker for ultimate Task04, not removal of required functionality.

Before ANY positive observer-money admissions a separately reviewed finite source-evidence extraction contract must provide: exact official provider/adapter/type source SHA+locations/version; method-specific supported raw result/chunk paths; exact own-data field/type/scalar categories schema; sorted enum/duplicate/conflict/unknown semantics; completeness across cache-read/cache-write/cancelled/inference/rejected/routing/surcharge and all attempts; correlation to raw ID/model/dispatch; usage-tail ordering; rejected/cancelled evidence without inferred local outcome; amount/currency semantic provenance; drift coverage; capture transcript revalidation. A hash-only categorySemanticProof without its exact predicate is insufficient. The future interface remains module-private extractMoneyNomination(ctx, verifiedTranscript, compiledAcceptedCategorySemantics), returning UNKNOWN(reason) or exact immutable categories bound to rawDigest/transcriptRef and actual raw amount/currency. It accepts no public label or proof choice. Until concrete official supported bytes and predicate pass independent design+source gates, only UNKNOWN is admissible. No present synthetic schema is asserted to be official.
